.TH UNIM-CLI 1 "April 2026" "UNIM 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unim\-cli \- Korean/English keyboard stream converter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unim\-cli
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FILE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B unim\-cli
is an offline batch utility that converts between English keyboard
character streams and composed Hangul. It is independent of the running
.B unim\-daemon
\(em it processes its input as a pure layout transformation.
.PP
With no input file, it reads from standard input. With one or more
.I FILE
arguments, files are processed in order and concatenated to standard
output (or the file given via
.BR \-o ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-compose
Compose an English keyboard stream into Hangul (default mode).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-decompose
Decompose Hangul into the equivalent English keyboard stream.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " "\-\-output \fIFILE\fR"
Write output to
.IR FILE
instead of standard output.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " "\-\-korean\-keyboard \fILAYOUT\fR"
Korean keyboard layout. One of
.BR 2bul ", " 390 ", " 391 ", " noshift "."
Default:
.BR 2bul "."
.TP
.BR \-e ", " "\-\-english\-keyboard \fILAYOUT\fR"
English keyboard layout. One of
.BR qwerty ", " dvorak ", " colemak ", " colemak_dh ", " workman "."
Default:
.BR qwerty "."
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Convert a stream of QWERTY keystrokes to Hangul:
.PP
.RS
.nf
echo "dkssudgktpdy" | unim\-cli \-c
.fi
.RE
.PP
Decompose a Hangul file into Dvorak keystrokes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
unim\-cli \-d \-e dvorak input.txt \-o keystrokes.txt
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unim (1),
.BR unim\-config (1)
